  <p>Caveats</p>
  <ul>
    <li>If <b>face</b> is <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/ALL_SIDES" target="_blank">ALL_SIDES</a> then the PRIM_GLTF_BASE_COLOR works on all sides.</li>
    <li>If <b>face</b> indicates a face that does not exist the PRIM_GLTF_BASE_COLOR return is an empty list.</li>
    <li><b>repeats</b> is not only used to get the number of repeats but the sign of the individual components indicate if "Flip" is set.</li>
    <li>In the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PRIM_TEXGEN_DEFAULT" target="_blank">default</a> <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PRIM_TEXGEN" target="_blank">texture mapping</a> <b>mode</b> the texture <b>repeats</b> units are in texture repeats per face. In the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PRIM_TEXGEN_PLANAR" target="_blank">planar</a> texture mapping mode the texture <b>repeats</b> units are in texture repeats per half meter. This is in contrast to the in-world editing tool, in which the planar texture scaling units are repeats per meter.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Target</p>
  <p>In the case of llGetPrimitiveParams is either the prim the script resides in, or the prim specified by the immediately prior <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PRIM_LINK_TARGET" target="_blank">PRIM_LINK_TARGET</a> call. However in the case of llGetLinkPrimitiveParams, it is either the value of the <b>link</b> parameter, or the prim specified by the immediately prior <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/PRIM_LINK_TARGET" target="_blank">PRIM_LINK_TARGET</a> call.</p>
